-NOTES = r"""
-Paper grounding and Step 0.  Section 1 fixes the exact definition: a fall
-k-coloring is a proper coloring in which every closed neighborhood contains
-all k colors.  The final section ("Fall colorings of complement of bipartite
-graphs") proves that, for bipartite G, a fall coloring of G^c consists of
-singletons for isolated vertices and the edges of a perfect matching on all
-positive-degree vertices.  This family uses no isolated vertices, so its
-certificates are exactly perfect matchings, represented as the resulting
-two-vertex fall-color classes.
-
-What makes it easy and the Track choice.  The same final theorem explicitly
-says recognition is polynomial-time because perfect matching is
-polynomial-time.  That rules out Track A before code is written.  This is
-therefore Track B and reports Hopcroft--Karp, O(E sqrt(V)), as a successful
-reference algorithm.  The compact route is different: the supplied successor
-permutations expose a simultaneous cyclic symmetry.  Once that invariant is
-noticed, any one edge incident with L_0 can be followed through the right
-successor cycle to write the entire matching in n-1 table applications.  The
-shipping preset stays below 300 such applications, whereas a generic matching
-implementation must at least read thousands of edge entries.
-
-Generation.  Independently shuffled full cycles are sampled on the left and
-right.  A random set of offsets is sampled, and every offset contributes one
-complete perfect-matching orbit.  The recorded answer is one of these orbits.
-Thus no search produces the certificate, and there is no special planted-edge
-population: every public edge belongs to an orbit with the same degree and
-matching status.  Relabeling either vertex class merely conjugates the two
-cycles and leaves the canonical offset pattern unchanged.
-
-Attacks.  Exact regularity defeats per-vertex degree outliers.  The shuffled
-labels defeat smallest- and largest-label greedy matching.  A 256-restart
-random greedy probe is measured at shipping size.  The hand-runnable ansatz
-that aligns the two successor cycles at their vertices numbered zero is
-excluded during generation, so it fails while other offsets remain valid.
-Hopcroft--Karp is not hidden among these failures: as Track B requires, it is
-reported separately and succeeds.
-""".strip()
